---
title: Music Recommender RAG System Architecture
---
flowchart TD
    Human(["👤 Human User\n(types natural language description)"])

    Human -->|free-text input| PARSE

    subgraph PARSE ["Piece 1 — Semantic Profile Parser (profile_parser.py)"]
        P1[Send description to Gemini API]
        P2[Gemini extracts structured profile\nfavorite_genre, favorite_mood,\ntarget_energy, likes_acoustic]
        P1 --> P2
    end

    P2 -->|structured profile dict| RETRIEVE

    subgraph RETRIEVE ["Piece 2 — Retriever (retrieval.py)"]
        R1[Load local songs.csv\n20 curated songs]
        R2[Fetch from Last.fm API\n~20 real songs by genre tag]
        R3[Combine into unified catalog\n~40 songs]
        R1 & R2 --> R3
    end

    R3 -->|combined catalog + profile| SCORE

    subgraph SCORE ["Scorer / Ranker (recommender.py)"]
        S1[score_song\naward points for genre, mood,\nenergy, acousticness match]
        S2[recommend_songs\nrank all songs, return top 5]
        S1 --> S2
    end

    S2 -->|top 5 songs + score reasons| EXPLAIN

    subgraph EXPLAIN ["Piece 3 — Explainer (recommender.py)"]
        E1[explain_recommendation\npass each song + original user\ndescription to Gemini API]
        E2[Gemini writes one natural-language\nsentence per song explaining the fit]
        E1 --> E2
    end

    E2 -->|final recommendations| OUTPUT(["📋 Output\nTop 5 songs ranked by score\nwith AI-generated explanations"])

    OUTPUT -->|human reviews results| Human

    subgraph TEST ["Testing & Reliability (tests/test_recommender.py)"]
        T1[test_recommend_returns_songs_sorted_by_score\nasserts top result matches genre + mood]
        T2[test_explain_recommendation_returns_non_empty_string\nasserts explanation is non-empty string]
        T3["Human Evaluation\n(manual spot-check: do recommendations\nmake sense for the description?)"]
    end

    SCORE -.->|pytest runs against Scorer| T1
    EXPLAIN -.->|pytest runs against Explainer| T2
    OUTPUT -.->|human inspects output| T3